Say X is numeric. Y is a factor. You're testing the hypothesis that the unweighted average of the effects of the levels of Y equals zero. This is a pretty ludicrous null hypothesis. 

> On Sep 20, 2016, at 12:27 PM, T. Florian Jaeger <timeguard-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org> wrote:
> 
> Guys,
